      [
       "b",
       "**Liquidity Order:** Currency, then Demand Deposits, then Savings Deposits, then Time Deposits.",
       "Indian Economy #38"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Note:** Cash is most liquid; fixed or time deposits are least liquid.",
       "Indian Economy #38"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Cash Withdrawal:** Withdraw 1 Lakh Rupee cash from Demand Deposit: Aggregate Money Supply does not change.",
       "Indian Economy #38"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Why:** Demand deposits drop by 1 Lakh, Currency with public rises by 1 Lakh.",
       "Indian Economy #38"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Money Multiplier:** Ratio of total money supply to base money (M3 divided by M0).",
       "Indian Economy #38"
      ],
      [
       "b",
       "**Effects:** Increase in banking habits increases the multiplier. Increase in CRR decreases credit creation.",
